# Quarto build output — regenerated by CI, never commit
/_site/
/.quarto/

# NOTE: _generated/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Quarto expands
# {{< include >}} while building the project context, which happens *before*
# pre-render scripts run — so the file has to exist in a clean checkout or the
# build fails. Committing it also means the last good publication list still
# publishes if the generator ever errors. It is refreshed on every render.

# Do commit /_freeze/ : it caches R chunk results so CI doesn't need R

# macOS
.DS_Store

# R
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

**/*.quarto_ipynb
